  "_comment": [
    "NIP-035 Ed25519 test vectors. Human-readable single source of truth;",
    "src/test/ed25519_tests.cpp mirrors these inline (drift between the",
    "two is treated as a consensus-affecting change, exactly like",
    "poseidon_vectors.json — see NIP-035 §8).",
    "",
    "rfc8032_pure_ed25519: canonical PureEd25519 KAT vectors from RFC 8032",
    "§7.1. The strict NIP-035 profile (non-cofactored verification, ",
    "canonical encodings, prime-order subgroup) accepts these unchanged.",
    "",
    "strict_reject: well-formed-size inputs that the strict profile",
    "rejects with a specific SCRIPT_ERR_ED25519_* category. These exist",
    "to catch backends that silently relax to ZIP-215."
  ],

